<p>On Monday, Apple released its second set of developer betas for its operating systems. (The final version of these releases should be available before the end of the year.) The big news this time is an update that directly addresses a shortcoming of the iPhone Duo, namely its lack of support for Face ID.</p>
<p>In the 27.3 beta, the iPhone Duo now supports &#8220;Unlock with Front Camera,&#8221; which is not the same as Face ID. Rather than using the Face ID method (which involves an infrared projector and sensor), iOS 27.3 is using the camera to look at your face. (This is presumably using a similar approach to how Apple <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/11/homeview-review-a-late-arrival-with-promise-but-still-showing-some-seams/">uses the camera in the HomeView</a> to authenticate your identity. Like HomeView, you&#8217;ll be prompted to look at the camera and then position your face up, down, left, and right.)</p>
<p>Since that&#8217;s fundamentally less secure than Face ID, there are a few wrinkles: It only works when there&#8217;s been a recent Touch ID or passcode authentication. Touch ID will still be required for Apple Pay, unlocking passwords, and after 45 minutes of inactivity. And it won&#8217;t work if you&#8217;re trying to unlock with the under-screen camera on the open Duo. (Turn it on by going to Touch ID &amp; Passcode in the Settings app.)</p>
<p>Still, that&#8217;s a pretty major tweak that partially addresses a point of friction on the Duo—namely, that it&#8217;s harder to unlock than other modern iPhones. In my time using the iPhone Duo I&#8217;ve gotten used to extra authentication, and using an Apple Watch has eased that process somewhat, but every little bit helps.</p>
<p>Another new Duo-related feature (under Display &amp; Brightness in the Settings app) is &#8220;close to lock iPhone Duo,&#8221; which gives users the option to have the Duo lock automatically when it&#8217;s closed. You could previously achieve this by using Shortcuts, but now Apple is making this option explicit. I can&#8217;t tell you how many times I&#8217;ve closed my Duo and felt I was declaring myself done with the device, only to realize it was still running and responding to careless touches.</p>
<p>Other new features include &#8220;ask about page,&#8221; which leverages the <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/11/safari-update-brings-vertical-tabs-adaptive-dark-mode-ai-integration/">just-introduced</a> AI integration in Safari to let you ask Siri to process and act on the entire content of a web page, not just the portion that&#8217;s visible on screen.</p>
<p>With this update, Apple has also added video podcasts from the Apple Podcasts library to the TV app, because what are video podcasts but TV with more visible microphones?</p>
